-- glycine, the simplest medium-dependent case. Atoms: 0 carboxyl carbon, 1 and 2 its oxygens, 3 the
-- alpha carbon, 4 and 5 its hydrogens, 6 the nitrogen. The alpha carbon carries the carboxyl, the amine
-- and two hydrogens, so substituting one of them makes it a stereocentre and the two products are
-- mirror images: the two hydrogens are enantiotopic. An achiral medium identifies them and a chiral one
-- does not.
num-gly-obs : List Nat
num-gly-obs = cons 4 (cons 5 nil)
